    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass, including the new `Cp34Tests`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature so the application fully satisfies the specification: *\"The request may include `birthDate` (ISO). When present, return `ageBand` as `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18-64) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against registrationDate.\"*\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):\n   - Added an optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) input field to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added a read-only `ageBand` enum field (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **Owner model** (`model/Owner.java`): Added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) with getter/setter. It maps automatically from the request DTO via MapStruct.\n\n3. **OwnerMapper** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`): Added a `deriveAgeBand(owner)` helper (mirroring the existing `locality`/`contactPreference` pattern) that returns `null` when no `birthDate` is present (so the field is omitted), otherwise computes whole years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` and maps to the band. It falls back to the current date if `registrationDate` is somehow absent \u2014 though the controller always defaults `registrationDate`.\n\n4. **DB schemas**: Added the `birth_date DATE` column to all four schema files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests, h2 \u2014 used at runtime, plus postgres and mysql for consistency).\n\nThe band boundaries follow the spec: `< 18` \u2192 MINOR, `18\u201364` \u2192 ADULT, `\u2265 65` \u2192 SENIOR. The new test `Cp34Tests` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT` against a `2026` registration date) passes, and all 46 pre-existing tests remain green.",
